WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Transcriber: TED Translators Admin
Reviewer: Mirjana Čutura

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.777
Fighting climate change has become
the greatest responsibility of our times.

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:21.833
And this is why in Europe,
we have set our objective:

00:00:21.857 --> 00:00:25.930
to become the first
carbon-neutral continent by 2050.

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:32.226
This means leading an entire continent
towards transitioning to clean energy,

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.986
reinventing our infrastructure,

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.713
and much, much more.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.952
It may sound abstract, and it sounds huge.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.690
And yes, it's actually both.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.673
And it is also possible.

00:00:46.356 --> 00:00:47.535
Why?

00:00:48.811 --> 00:00:49.967
In the European Union,

00:00:49.991 --> 00:00:53.936
we have a good record
of turning ambitions into successes.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:57.614
We are a political and economic union

00:00:57.638 --> 00:00:59.205
with 27 countries

00:00:59.229 --> 00:01:03.341
and the total population
of 450 million people.

00:01:04.351 --> 00:01:10.271
On the ashes of two world wars,
we have secured lasting peace among us.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:15.340
From a divided continent,
we have created a union without borders.

00:01:15.686 --> 00:01:19.778
And I strongly believe
we can also achieve our next challenge:

00:01:19.802 --> 00:01:22.902
becoming the first
carbon-neutral continent.

00:01:23.424 --> 00:01:25.896
When I became president
of the European Commission,

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.903
I sent a clear signal.

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:31.693
In the first two weeks,
I tabled the European Green Deal.

00:01:32.889 --> 00:01:34.586
This European Green Deal

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:38.646
is both our vision
for a climate-neutral continent

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:41.633
and a very dedicated
road map to this goal.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:46.116
It is 50 actions for 2050,

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:50.396
ranging from the first-ever
European climate law,

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:52.286
to circular economy,

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:54.651
to a biodiversity strategy,

00:01:54.675 --> 00:01:56.336
planting trees,

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.976
protecting precious nature and animals,

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.790
recycling and waste management,

00:02:01.814 --> 00:02:03.314
just to name a few.

00:02:04.797 --> 00:02:07.686
When the coronavirus pandemic hit,

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:11.373
we resolved not to let
our objective be derailed.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:15.268
The economic and social crisis
created by the pandemic

00:02:15.292 --> 00:02:17.186
cannot be an excuse

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:22.330
to postpone the transition
towards a cleaner and healthier future.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.036
On the opposite,

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:30.360
they create an additional accelerator
to mobilize and to move ahead.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:34.177
Of course, not everyone agreed.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.806
Some in the industry
told us it was impossible

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.833
to remain competitive
under these new constraints.

00:02:41.607 --> 00:02:46.610
Some unions were afraid jobs would be lost
and workers forgotten.

00:02:47.304 --> 00:02:50.013
Some politicians said
it was not realistic.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:53.526
We listened to them,

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:57.716
but we also listened
to other facts and arguments:

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:02.206
the large international support
to the Paris Agreement,

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:07.566
science with robust data,
and more data every year,

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:11.086
the evidence of climate
shifting all around us.

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:12.926
We all know it by now:

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.166
glaciers melting, forest fires,

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.276
more extreme weather events.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.576
And this is just the beginning.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:26.334
We saw the prospect of many new jobs
created by the transition;

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:30.976
European citizens,
who, in their overwhelming majority,

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:36.206
consider that climate change
is a very serious problem;

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.526
our youth demanding
action for their future,

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:40.903
and rightly so.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.646
Building on this, in September 2020,

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:48.586
we announced we would go one step further.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:54.466
We moved from a 40 percent reduction
of greenhouse gas emissions by 2030

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:58.753
to an at least 55 percent
reduction by 2030.

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:03.750
We are taking this bold
commitment for two reasons.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:08.387
First, we already know
that we need to push further

00:04:08.411 --> 00:04:12.416
if we're serious about reaching
our 2050 objective,

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:13.663
which we are.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:19.693
And second, the more we progress,
the more we rally.

00:04:20.364 --> 00:04:24.267
Our 2030 and 2050
time lines are ambitious.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:26.813
They are also necessary.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:32.857
Solving climate change
will help solve a host of other problems.

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:37.635
Ignoring it will only precipitate them,

00:04:37.659 --> 00:04:41.016
as we see with the link
between the loss of biodiversity

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:43.973
and zoonotic viruses like the coronavirus.

00:04:45.376 --> 00:04:49.726
I know some are concerned
with this transition,

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:53.820
and I want to tell them
these concerns are legitimate.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:55.906
But we have the knowledge,

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:58.136
we have the technology,

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.801
we have now the resources
to accompany this change

00:05:00.825 --> 00:05:03.338
and make this transition just.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.856
We are directing our recovery
in this direction.

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.068
If we get it right,

00:05:10.092 --> 00:05:14.856
a third of our recovery money,
called Next Generation EU,

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.336
and of our long-term budget

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:21.190
will go to climate goals
and climate projects.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:25.693
And this is more than 600 billion euros.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.586
Now, addressing climate change

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:32.706
will need more than politicians
and more than a continent.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:37.639
States, companies,
cities, citizens everywhere

00:05:37.663 --> 00:05:39.304
need to move in the same direction

00:05:39.328 --> 00:05:42.363
and to sustain their action
over the long term.

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:45.006
The European Union is open to cooperate

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:48.203
with anyone who's ready
to engage in this journey.

00:05:48.997 --> 00:05:53.990
Fixing climate change
calls for everyone's action every day.

00:05:54.718 --> 00:05:56.248
You can count on me.

00:05:56.605 --> 00:05:58.425
I count on you.

00:05:58.821 --> 00:06:00.000
Thank you.

